# Runtime state is deliberately not versioned.
#
# It is 322MB and growing every 180s: state/raw alone is 161MB of MCP response
# dumps and state/tool_calls.ndjson is 144MB of append-only call trace. Committing
# it would make every author-agent commit enormous, and the launchd agents write to
# it continuously, so the index would never be clean. The ledgers are already
# append-only and immutable on disk, which is the property we actually wanted from
# version control here.
#
# No trailing slash, and anchored. `state/` would match only a directory, and the
# author agent's worktrees link state in as a *symlink* -- which `git add -A` then
# happily committed, putting a machine-specific absolute path into the tree and from
# there into every published release. Caught by the vcs self-test on 2026-08-25.
/state

# Immutable release trees and the live pointer. These are *outputs* of a commit,
# published by deploy/release.sh. Versioning them would store every file twice and
# let a stale release tree be resurrected by a checkout, which is precisely the
# confusion the release/ symlink exists to prevent.
/releases
/release

# Build and editor noise.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.tmp
*.tmp.[0-9]*

# Generated previews and operator evidence, rebuilt/appended locally.
game-preview.html
/farm-strategy-journal.md

# Local scratch that must never reach a commit.
.author-stage-*/
*.local.json
state/alerts.ndjson.pre-batchid-purge
